> Thanks for the logs.
>
> Registers show xHC and the command ring are running, but it still didn't =
process the
> 'enable slot' command. There are no command completion events on the even=
t ring.
> No interrupts either, but that is expected as there are no events.
>
> Odd thing is that event ring is completely empty.
> There's usually a port change event when host detects a device, this even=
t triggers
> hub driver to start the usb device enumeration process, queuing the 'enab=
le slot'
> command as one of the first steps.
>
> Either xHC isn't really running, or fails to write to the event ring.
>
> I noticed that both event and command rings DMA addresses are above 32 bi=
t.
>
> Maybe dmesg log with usb core and xhci dynamic debug enabled could show s=
omething.
> Can you add the following to the kernel cmd line:
>
> xhci_hcd.dyndbg=3D+p usbcore.dyndbg=3D+p
>
> Could also be worth testing with with 32bit DMA mask:
>
> xhci_hcd.quirks=3D0x800000
>
>
> Details from slot_200 logs;
> reg-op
> USBCMD =3D 0x00000005     xHC is Running with interrupts enabled,
> USBSTS =3D 0x00000010     port change detect active, EINT=3D=3D0 so no un=
handled interrupt pending.
> CRCR =3D 0x00000008       command ring is running
>
> reg-runtime
> MFINDEX =3D 0x00003252
> IR0_IMAN =3D 0x00000002      primary interrupter enabled
> IR0_ERDP_LOW =3D 0x026d3000  event ring dma address has both high and low=
 32 bit values
> IR0_ERDP_HIGH =3D 0x00000001
>
> command-ring/trbs
>   0 0x00000001026d1000: Enable Slot Command: flags C
>   0 0x00000001026d1010: type 'UNKNOWN' -> raw 00000000 00000000 00000000 =
00000000
>
> event-ring/trbs
>   0 0x00000001026d3000: type 'UNKNOWN' -> raw 00000000 00000000 00000000 =
00000000
>   0 0x00000001026d3010: type 'UNKNOWN' -> raw 00000000 00000000 00000000 =
00000000
>
> Event ring is empty, command ring shows the Enable Slot command that time=
s out.
>
> Thanks
> Mathias

